I wonder if you could use {bo} to link UI...  With regard to the
realis/irrealis, I'm still a little fuzzy on the difference between the two,
but I believe the CLL makes a distinction between "pure emotions" and
"propositional attitude indicators".  I think chapter 13.3 says it best:

As mentioned at the beginning of Section
2<http://www.lojban.org/publications/reference_grammar/chapter13.html#s2>,
attitudinals may be divided into two groups, the pure emotion indicators
explained in that section, and a contrasting group which may be called the
``propositional attitude indicators''. These indicators establish an
internal, hypothetical world which the speaker is reacting to, distinct from
the world as it really is. Thus we may be expressing our attitude towards
``what the world would be like if ...'', or more directly stating our
attitude towards making the potential world a reality.

On Wed, Oct 13, 2010 at 1:50 PM, Lindar <lindarthebard@yahoo.com> wrote:

> From the department of Shut Up You Emo Fag comes a question about UI.
